### Chat Backend REST Client Specification
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@contentType = application/json

### 0. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###

### 1. List All Users
# @name listUsers
GET {{baseUrl}}/user
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###

### 2. Create User 1 (Alice)
# @name createAlice
POST {{baseUrl}}/user/create
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Alice Smith",
  "email": "alice.demo@example.com"
}

###

### 3. Create User 2 (Bob)
# @name createBob
POST {{baseUrl}}/user/create
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Bob Jones",
  "email": "bob.demo@example.com"
}

###

### 4. Create or Get Direct Chat (API 1)
# @name createDirectChat
# Replace userAId and userBId with actual user IDs from create user / list users
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/create
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "userAId": "0f3ef420-9509-455f-8afc-0803cf8f62a0",
  "userBId": "6fb6ca7a-a3cc-44c3-9bab-c67ab5858c1a"
}

###

### 5. Send Message (API 2)
# Replace chatId and senderId with actual IDs
@chatId = 94842f95-991e-4915-a203-0e0fcae961d0
@aliceId = 0f3ef420-9509-455f-8afc-0803cf8f62a0
@bobId = 6fb6ca7a-a3cc-44c3-9bab-c67ab5858c1a

# @name sendMessage
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/{{chatId}}/message/send
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "senderId": "{{aliceId}}",
  "text": "Hello Bob! Testing real-time message storage in Firestore."
}

###

### 6. Get Messages with Limit & Ordering (API 3)
# @name getMessages
GET {{baseUrl}}/chat/{{chatId}}/messages?limit=50&userId={{aliceId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###

### 7. Mark Message Read (API 4)
# Replace messageId with actual message ID returned from sendMessage or getMessages
@messageId = YPwGxEB6SwDbFAJ8BlDl

# @name markMessageRead
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/{{chatId}}/message/{{messageId}}/read
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "userId": "{{bobId}}"
}

###

### 8. Update Last Seen Message (API 5)
# @name updateLastSeen
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/{{chatId}}/lastseen
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "userId": "{{bobId}}",
  "messageId": "{{messageId}}"
}

###

### 9. List User Chats with Member IDs & Message Previews (API 6)
# @name listUserChats
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/{{aliceId}}/chats
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###

### 10. Bonus: Create Group Chat
# @name createGroupChat
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat/group/create
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "creatorId": "{{aliceId}}",
  "name": "Backend Team Sprint",
  "memberIds": [
    "{{bobId}}",
    "4f26c865-f66d-41cb-9811-762b42db1511"
  ]
}

###

### 11. Bonus: Edit Message
# @name editMessage
PUT {{baseUrl}}/chat/{{chatId}}/message/{{messageId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "userId": "{{aliceId}}",
  "text": "Hello Bob! Testing updated text (edited)."
}

###

### 12. Bonus: Delete Message (Soft Delete)
# @name deleteMessage
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/chat/{{chatId}}/message/{{messageId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "userId": "{{aliceId}}"
}

